# Cursor Editor — Secure Agent Behavior

## Overview

Cursor implements multiple layers of safety and security controls to prevent the agent from performing harmful actions, generating dangerous content, or bypassing established security boundaries. These controls operate independently of user-defined Rules and Skills.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[User prompt received] --> B[Content Filter Check]
    B --> C{Content passes filters?}
    C -->|No| D[Block request + notify user]
    C -->|Yes| E[Security Boundary Check]
    E --> F{Passes security checks?}
    F -->|No| G[Block request + notify user]
    F -->|Yes| H[Agent Reasoning]
    H --> I[Tool Selection]
    I --> J{Tool requires escalation?}
    J -->|Yes| K[Ask user for approval]
    J -->|No| L[Execute tool]
    K --> M{User approves?}
    M -->|Yes| L
    M -->|No| D
    L --> N{Result safe?}
    N -->|Yes| O[Continue]
    N -->|No| P[Self-correct + escalate]
```

---

## Red-Team Protections

### What Agents Are Blocked From Doing

Cursor's built-in safety system prevents the agent from performing these actions regardless of user prompt:

| Blocked Action | Category | Reason |
|---------------|----------|--------|
| **Modify core files** | File protection | Prevents breaking Cursor/IDE internals |
| **Bypass authentication** | Security | Never generates auth bypass code |
| **Access system files** | File protection | Prevents reading `/etc/passwd`, etc. |
| **Delete system directories** | File protection | Prevents catastrophic data loss |
| **Modify other users' files** | Permission | Respects file ownership |
| **Execute as root/SUDO** | Security | Prevents privilege escalation |
| **Generate malware** | Content safety | Never creates malicious code |
| **Exfiltrate data** | Data safety | Prevents data leakage to unknown endpoints |
| **Bypass rate limits** | Security integrity | Maintains system integrity |
| **Access credentials** | Secret protection | Never reads/writes credential files |

### Core File Protection

Certain directories and files are protected from modification:

```
Protected paths (examples):
  /usr/bin/*
  /usr/lib/*
  /etc/shadow
  ~/.ssh/authorized_keys
  ~/.gnupg/*
  /etc/passwd
  /etc/sudoers
```

Protected directories in the project:
```
Core project paths that require approval:
  core/*
  infra/*
  .cursor/*  (agent configuration)
  node_modules/*
  .git/*
```

### Authentication Bypass Prevention

The agent will never generate code that:

| Action | Example | Why Blocked |
|--------|---------|-------------|
| Skips auth checks | `// Skip authentication` | Security violation |
| Hardcodes admin tokens | `const adminToken = "..."` | Credential exposure |
| Disables security | `app.disable('helmet')` | Security downgrade |
| Bypasses JWT validation | `if (true) return user` | Auth bypass |
| Opens CORS fully | `cors({ origin: '*' })` | Security misconfiguration |

