## Safety Guardrails

### Agent Safety Rules

These guardrails operate automatically and cannot be disabled by user configuration:

| Guardrail | Description | Enforcement |
|-----------|-------------|-------------|
| **No credential exposure** | Never outputs API keys, tokens, passwords | Automatic block |
| **No auth bypass** | Never generates authentication circumvention | Automatic block |
| **No harmful code** | Never generates malware or attack tools | Automatic block |
| **No data exfiltration** | Never sends data to unknown endpoints | Automatic block |
| **No privilege escalation** | Never executes commands requiring elevated permissions | Requires approval |
| **File system boundaries** | Cannot write outside workspace by default | Automatic block |
| **Network boundaries** | Cannot connect to unknown external services | Requires approval |
| **Database safety** | Cannot DROP/DELETE without explicit confirmation | Requires approval |

### File System Guardrails

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Agent wants to write file] --> B{Path in workspace?}
    B -->|Yes| C{Path in protected dirs?}
    B -->|No| D[Block + notify]
    C -->|No| E[Allow write]
    C -->|Yes| F[Require user approval]
    
    D --> G[Error: Path outside workspace]
    F --> H{User approves?}
    H -->|Yes| E
    H -->|No| G
```

### Database Safety Guardrails

The agent requires explicit approval for destructive database operations:

| Operation | Default Behavior | Can Be Overridden? |
|-----------|-----------------|-------------------|
| `SELECT` | Allowed | No (always safe) |
| `INSERT` | Allowed | No |
| `UPDATE` | Allowed | No |
| `DELETE` | Ask confirmation | Yes |
| `DROP TABLE` | Blocked | No |
| `DROP DATABASE` | Blocked | No |
| `TRUNCATE` | Blocked | No |
| `ALTER TABLE` | Ask confirmation | Yes |

